ion","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.quarkNumber","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L133-L135","doc":"`+1` for a quark strand, `-1` for an antiquark strand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.charge3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.charge3","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L129-L131","doc":"Three times the electric charge (imported SM values). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instReprStrand.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instReprStrand.repr","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instReprStrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instReprStrand","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instDecidableEqStrand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.instDecidableEqStrand","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.dbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.dbar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.ubar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.ubar","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.d","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand.u","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.Strand","kind":"inductive","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L122-L125","doc":"Strand labels: two flavours of quark and their antiquarks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_crossing_not_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_crossing_not_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L110-L116","doc":"**The factor-wise crossing on a two-factor strand space obeys no Hecke relation for\n`1 < q`**: no `a, b` make all three eigenvalues `q², -1, q⁻²` roots of `x² = a x + b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_hecke_eigenvalues_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_hecke_eigenvalues_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L94-L108","doc":"For `1 < q`, the three eigenvalues `q², -1, q⁻²` of `R_A ⊗ R_B` are pairwise distinct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.three_eigenvalues_no_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.three_eigenvalues_no_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L75-L86","doc":"Three pairwise distinct elements cannot all satisfy one monic quadratic `x² = a x + b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_eigenvalue_not_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuarkStrandConsequences.tensor_eigenvalue_not_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuarkStrandConsequences.lean#L61-L73","doc":"The product eigenvalue `q²` is a Hecke eigenvalue at `q` (i.e. `q` or `-q⁻¹`) only if\n`q = 1` or `q³ = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}